Chunk the K-pool indexer logits in _get_topk_ragged_kpool_plan by query rows.

Base: sgl-project/sglang d6ab04bdf1 (the pinned image), file
python/sglang/srt/layers/attention/dsa/dsa_indexer_kpool.py
(SHA-256 5a841692d4721f9a55a2dbcd1dc39abddfec5fb7a1207922221e9ad93af6eec2).
Result: SHA-256 89cdb6933ef024d1bc596c016cadd0ca989878964405a2770c9e139c476614f0.
The September 27 servers ran this diff plus kpool-logits-verify.diff (verify
mode off), SHA-256 58e59be00ad2bec6bc28901d72c2a53853df2bc9635a9528d23528a1764a107e.
The code is published exactly as it ran.

Upstream fixed the same defect in sgl-project/sglang#40854 (merged
2026-09-26), which chunks this path and the per-request path under the
existing free-memory budget. Prefer an image that includes it.

Scope and caveats of this local diff:
- Only _get_topk_ragged_kpool_plan is chunked. _get_topk_ragged_kpool and
  _get_topk_ragged_with_cp still allocate their logits unchunked.
- Chunking is skipped when get_is_capture_mode() is true. At d6ab04bdf1 that
  includes breakable CUDA graph segments; #40854 gates on
  torch.cuda.is_current_stream_capturing() instead. In the reference
  configuration SGLang disables prefill CUDA graphs for this model ("Breakable
  CUDA graph is incompatible with KDA hybrid linear attention"), so extend
  batches run eagerly and the budget applies.
- Budget: the smaller of SGLANG_DSA_KPOOL_LOGITS_BUDGET_MB (default 4096),
  half of free plus reusable cached device memory, and 30% of total device
  memory, applied only when rows x columns reaches 8,000,000 (FP32, 4 bytes
  per element). Row bytes ignore DeepGEMM's column alignment.
- The in-code comment "per-row results are unchanged" means each row's scores
  depend only on that row's inputs. Scores were bit-identical in the check;
  identical top-k selections were not shown, because the unpatched top-k
  itself varies on tied scores.
- No log line records when chunking engages.

